'''breading†''', ''n.'' [< ''bread''<sup>2</sup> + ''-ing''<sup>1</sup>.] A windrow or swath. [Prov. Eng.] See extract.
{{smaller block|''Breadings'' of corn or grass, the swathes or lows wherein the mower leaves them.
{{right|''Kennett'' (Halliwell).}}}}

